{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01CH178jfFrcfFW1Z2ZVcf1b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Aurora â€” what this project IS\n\n- **An autonomous discovery-and-curation system for the open-source Claude/agent ecosystem.** It runs three nightly multi-agent \"sweeps\" â€” Skills (23:00), Tools (00:00), and Agents (22:00) â€” that discover, validate, and catalog skills, tools, and agents. *(CLAUDE.md \"Aurora at a glance\")*\n\n- **It ships a knowledge base + browsable library.** Outputs are a SQLite KB (`kb/aurora.db`) and a generated `library/` of per-artifact pages (the working tree shows hundreds of `library/agents/*` and `library/models/*` index pages). *(CLAUDE.md; git status)*\n\n- **It produces recurring reports for the user.** Nightly exec summaries (`reports/`), a morning briefing (08:30) with a machine-readable `reports/morning/latest_summary.json` carrying a productivity index, cost rollups, find counts, and self-healing upgrades. *(CLAUDE.md Â§4 \"Ingest Aurora State\")*\n\n- **It publishes a scrubbed snapshot to a private distribution repo.** A nightly publisher (~01:45) pushes a sanitized tag to the `aurora-library` repo; source lives in `aurora-source`. *(CLAUDE.md \"Aurora at a glance\" / \"Key files\")*\n\n- **It surfaces its catalog into live Claude sessions via \"Helping Hand.\"** A Cowork/Claude Code plugin + `aurora-kb` MCP server recommends matching skills/templates/tools/agents on session start and per request (the GWL score-gate protocol). *(CLAUDE.md Â§2)*\n\n- **Core machinery is Python orchestration.** `orchestrator.py` (sweep entry, `--sweep {skills,tools,agents}`), `llm.py` (all LLM calls funnel here, with retry/degrade logic), `publisher.py`, plus scheduled-task setup (`bin/setup-tasks.ps1`) and plugin builds (`bin/build-plugin.py`). *(CLAUDE.md \"Key files\")*\n\n- **Current direction (per memory/git):** an \"awareness revamp\" reframing Aurora as an agentic-AI awareness/decision instrument, plus a read-only Flask dashboard (`dashboard/`, port 5001) shipped 2026-06-11. The active branch `foreman/aurora-revamp` shows W2â€“W5 revamp commits. *(MEMORY.md; recent commits)*\n\nThese are grounded in the project's own `CLAUDE.md`, memory index, and git state. I did not open the source files to verify the runtime behavior â€” say the word and I'll confirm any specific claim (e.g., that `orchestrator.py` actually implements the three sweeps) against the code."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4419,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7405,"cache_read_input_tokens":20597,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":7405},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e136e478-1d35-4067-8d5f-3834f3bd708d","uuid":"8cedcbf6-9235-4963-907e-421eb2d47789","request_id":"req_011Cc1epdAwqJUgWrTs6YDA5"}
